conwayPolynomial -- provide a Conway polynomial
***********************************************

Description
===========

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        conwayPolynomial(q,Variable=>a)
  * Inputs:
      * q, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a power of a prime number
      * a, a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, an optional input, the symbol
        served as variable, default a
  * Outputs:
      * a Conway polynomial whose roots generate a field with q elements
+-------------------------+
|i1 : conwayPolynomial 125|
|                         |
|      3                  |
|o1 = a  - 2a - 2         |
|                         |
|     ZZ                  |
|o1 : --[a]               |
|      5                  |
+-------------------------+

Synopsis
========

  * Usage: 
        conwayPolynomial(p,n,Variable=>a)
  * Inputs:
      * p, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a prime number
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
      * a, a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, an optional input, the symbol
        served as variable, default a
  * Outputs:
      * a Conway polynomial whose roots generate a field with p^n elements
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : conwayPolynomial(2,20,Variable=>"b")      |
|                                               |
|      20    10    9    7    6    5    4        |
|o2 = b   + b   + b  + b  + b  + b  + b  + b + 1|
|                                               |
|     ZZ                                        |
|o2 : --[b]                                     |
|      2                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------+

Ways to use conwayPolynomial:
=============================

  * "conwayPolynomial(ZZ)"
  * "conwayPolynomial(ZZ,ZZ)"

For the programmer
==================

